 ('ENT_MON_STYMPHALIAN_BIRDS','PER_GRK_ARCHAIC','Man-eating bronze-beaked birds of Lake Stymphalia driven off by Heracles in his sixth labour. Attested Apollodorus 2.5.6; Pausanias 8.22.4. Collective entity.'),
 ('ENT_MON_GRAEAE','PER_GRK_ARCHAIC','Grey-haired sisters (Deino, Enyo, Pemphredo) sharing one eye and one tooth, daughters of Phorcys and Ceto; coerced by Perseus. Attested Hesiod, Theogony 270-273; Apollodorus 2.4.2. Collective entity.'),
 ('ENT_MON_HECATONCHEIRES','PER_GRK_ARCHAIC','The hundred-handed, fifty-headed giants Cottus, Briareus and Gyges, sons of Ouranos and Gaia; allies of Zeus against the Titans and jailers of the imprisoned Titans. Attested Hesiod, Theogony 147-153, 617-735. Collective entity.'),
 ('ENT_MON_GIGANTES','PER_GRK_ARCHAIC','Earth-born giants sprung from Gaia (from the blood of Ouranos) who warred on the Olympians in the Gigantomachy. Attested Hesiod, Theogony 183-186; Apollodorus 1.6.1-2. Collective entity.'),
 ('ENT_MON_NIDHOGGR','PER_NOR_VIKING','Corpse-devouring dragon-serpent that gnaws the root of Yggdrasil from below in Niflheim/Náströnd. Attested Poetic Edda, Völuspá 39, 66 and Grímnismál 32, 35; Snorri, Prose Edda (Gylfaginning). Norse functional cognate of the Greek chthonic monster-serpent.');
INSERT INTO entity_periods (entity_id,period_id,confidence,rationale,source_id,review_status)
INSERT INTO _r VALUES
 ('ENT_MON_ECHIDNA','paired_with','ENT_TYPHON','high','Hesiod, Theog. 306-308: Echidna couples with Typhon (Typhaon) to bear the monster brood. paired_with (not consort_of, which is not a valid type).'),
 ('ENT_MON_ECHIDNA','parent_of','ENT_MON_ORTHRUS','high','Hesiod, Theog. 309-310: Echidna bore Orthrus the hound of Geryon.'),
 ('ENT_MON_ECHIDNA','parent_of','ENT_CERBERUS','high','Hesiod, Theog. 310-312: Echidna bore Cerberus, the brazen-voiced hound of Hades (existing entity).'),
 ('ENT_MON_ECHIDNA','parent_of','ENT_HYDRA','high','Hesiod, Theog. 313-315: Echidna bore the Lernaean Hydra (existing entity).'),
 ('ENT_MON_ECHIDNA','parent_of','ENT_CHIMERA','medium','Hesiod, Theog. 319-325: the Chimera in the prevailing reading belongs to the Echidna/Typhon line (variant: of Echidna and Orthrus). Existing entity.'),
 ('ENT_TYPHON','parent_of','ENT_MON_ORTHRUS','high','Hesiod, Theog. 306-310: Typhon father of Echidna''s brood, including Orthrus.'),
 ('ENT_TYPHON','parent_of','ENT_CERBERUS','high','Hesiod, Theog. 306-312: Typhon father of Cerberus by Echidna (existing entity).'),
 ('ENT_TYPHON','parent_of','ENT_HYDRA','high','Hesiod, Theog. 306-315: Typhon father of the Hydra by Echidna (existing entity).'),
 ('ENT_MON_ORTHRUS','sibling_of','ENT_CERBERUS','high','Hesiod, Theog. 309-312: Orthrus and Cerberus both born of Typhon and Echidna (existing entity).'),
 ('ENT_MON_ORTHRUS','guardian_of','ENT_GERYON','high','Hesiod, Theog. 309-311; Apollodorus 2.5.10: Orthrus guarded the cattle of Geryon and was slain by Heracles (existing entity).'),
 ('ENT_MON_SPHINX','child_of','ENT_MON_ORTHRUS','medium','Hesiod, Theog. 326-327: the Sphinx (Phix) born of Orthrus (contested maternal line).'),
 ('ENT_MON_SPHINX','child_of','ENT_CHIMERA','medium','Hesiod, Theog. 326-329: the Sphinx and Nemean Lion born of the Chimera (by Orthrus) per one construal. Existing entity.'),
 ('ENT_NEMEAN_LION','child_of','ENT_CHIMERA','medium','Hesiod, Theog. 327-329: the Nemean Lion in the same brood-line, connected to the Chimera/Orthrus. Both existing entities.'),
 ('ENT_MON_NIDHOGGR','dwells_in','ENT_NOR_YGGDRASIL','high','Poetic Edda, Grímnismál 32, 35 and Völuspá 66: Níðhöggr gnaws the root of Yggdrasil from below (existing entity).'),
 ('ENT_MON_NIDHOGGR','aligned_with','ENT_MON_ECHIDNA','low','Modern comparative cross-tradition pairing: Níðhöggr as the Norse functional cognate of the Greek chthonic monster-serpent of the Echidna brood (aligned_with = modern functional analogue, not ancient identification).'),
 ('ENT_MON_GRAEAE','aligned_with','ENT_MON_SIRENS','low','Structural grouping within the wider chthonic Phorcys/Ceto and sea-monster cohort of early Greek myth (Gantz, Early Greek Myth); cohort linkage, NOT attested kinship (changed from sibling_of, which would falsely assert shared parentage).'),
 ('ENT_MON_HECATONCHEIRES','opposes','ENT_MON_GIGANTES','low','Structural contrast among Gaia''s primordial earth-born hosts: the Hundred-Handers fight for Zeus, while the Gigantes war against the Olympians (Hesiod, Theog.; Apollodorus 1.6).'),
 ('ENT_MON_STYMPHALIAN_BIRDS','aligned_with','ENT_MON_HARPIES','low','Comparative grouping of monstrous bird-collectives of Greek myth (Stymphalian Birds, Harpies, Sirens); cohort linkage for graph connectivity, not genealogical kinship.');
